-- title:
--   Proposition 4.7 — regret of the Multiplicative Weights Algorithm (Arora et al., Theorem 2.1)
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal X$ be a finite action space, $T$ a horizon and $\ell_{i,t}\in[-1,1]$ ($i\in\mathcal X$, $t=1,\dots,T$) losses. Let $p_t$ be the distributions generated by the Multiplicative Weights Algorithm with learning rate $\gamma\in(0,1/2]$ against these losses. Then for every fixed $j\in\mathcal X$,
--   $$\sum_{t=1}^T\langle p_t,\ell_t\rangle\le\sum_{t=1}^T\ell_{j,t}+\gamma\sum_{t=1}^T|\ell_{j,t}|+\frac{\log|\mathcal X|}\gamma .$$
--
--   In the proof of Lemma 4.6 it is applied to OneRound's table updates with decisions $(v,a')$, losses $-h/H$ and learning rate $\eta H$.
--
--   **Formalization Note** Rounds are indexed $0,\dots,T-1$. The loss sequence is arbitrary, which covers losses chosen after $p_t$ is played.
--
--   Differences from the source:
--   - encoding: learning rate $\gamma\le1/2$ → $0<\gamma\le1/2$; reason: a learning rate is positive; the bound divides by $\gamma$
--   - encoding: "the Multiplicative Weights Algorithm" → weights $w_1\equiv1$, $w_{t+1}(i)=w_t(i)(1-\gamma\ell_{i,t})$, $p_t=w_t/\sum w_t$; reason: the algorithm of Arora–Hazan–Kale's Theorem 2.1, and the update the paper uses on p.21
--   - encoding: losses $\{\ell_{i,t}\}_{i\in\mathcal X,t\in[T]}$ in $[-1,1]$, rounds $1,\dots,T$ → a sequence $\ell:\mathbb N\to\mathcal X\to\mathbb R$ with values in $[-1,1]$ at every $t$, rounds $0,\dots,T-1$; reason: only $t<T$ enters the statement, and any losses on $[T]$ extend (e.g. by $0$) to such a sequence
-- source:
--   Brüstle, di Gregorio, Fusco, Leonardi, Regret Bounds for Profit Maximization in Bilateral Trade: Learning the Best Posted-Price Mechanism (manuscript, STOC 2027 submission, sha256 e91e81279505b765c7c96c219d674c0fbbbd6ca47a00da8fe228d498ca25ac87), Proposition 4.7, p.21 (PDF 23), quoting Arora, Hazan, Kale, The Multiplicative Weights Update Method: a Meta-Algorithm and Applications, Theory of Computing 8 (2012), Theorem 2.1

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_BilateralProfit_MWU

namespace BilateralProfit

/-- **Proposition 4.7** (Theorem 2.1 of Arora, Hazan, Kale), Brüstle, di Gregorio, Fusco,
Leonardi (manuscript, sha256 e91e8127…), p.21 (PDF 23): for losses `ℓ_{i,t} ∈ [−1, 1]` over a
finite action space `𝒳` and horizon `T`, the distributions `p_t` of the Multiplicative Weights
Algorithm with learning rate `γ ≤ 1/2` satisfy, for every fixed `j ∈ 𝒳`,
`Σ_t ⟨p_t, ℓ_t⟩ ≤ Σ_t ℓ_{j,t} + γ Σ_t |ℓ_{j,t}| + log|𝒳|/γ`.

**Formalization Note.** Rounds are `t = 0, …, T − 1`. `𝒳` is a finite type (nonempty, as it contains `j`); `γ > 0`
(the bound divides by `γ`). The loss sequence is arbitrary, which covers losses chosen after
seeing `p_t`. -/
theorem proposition_4_7 {X : Type} [Fintype X] (γ : ℝ) (hγ : 0 < γ)
    (hγ' : γ ≤ 1 / 2) (T : ℕ) (ℓ : ℕ → X → ℝ) (hℓ : ∀ t i, ℓ t i ∈ Set.Icc (-1 : ℝ) 1) (j : X) :
    ∑ t ∈ Finset.range T, ∑ i, mwDist γ ℓ t i * ℓ t i ≤
      ∑ t ∈ Finset.range T, ℓ t j + γ * ∑ t ∈ Finset.range T, |ℓ t j| +
        Real.log (Fintype.card X) / γ := by sorry

end BilateralProfit
